"""On-demand host-independent contract; does not read or write memory."""

def memory_help():
    return {
        'actions': {
            'search':{'query':'original question text','subquestions':'optional array of at most 3 explicit questions; preserve the original subject, scope and conditions; never insert guessed answers','intent':'optional brief clarification of the asked aspect; never authority or permission','include_assistant':'optional boolean; defaults false','include_history':'optional boolean; defaults false; explicitly discover retired notes'},
            'get':{'id':'note id; never a source id','offset':'optional nonnegative integer; explicit 0 starts 4000-character pagination, then follow next_offset'},
            'source':{'id':'source id','version':'optional integer','offset':'start at 0, then returned next_offset'},
            'drafts':{'limit':'1..50','offset':'0..1000000','include_closed':'optional boolean','draft_id':'optional'},
            'remember':'search first, then write a new note',
            'amend':{'id':'current owned note id','expected_version':'integer; same baseline on retry','search_id':'fresh search id','statement_changes':'optional array of {old: exact unique passage, new: replacement}; unchanged text is preserved','condition_changes':'optional array of {old: complete exact condition, new: replacement or null to remove}','add_conditions':'optional new condition strings','evidence':'new source_id/version/quote entries; existing evidence is retained','revision_reason':'required explanation; existing hypothesis/new-evidence guards still apply','correction_event_ids':'optional exact effective correction event keys'},
            'update':'search and get first; submit a full proposal with get.id/key/topic and current version as expected_version; preserve metadata.scope and metadata.content_type',
            'resolve':{'draft_id':'id','decision':'retry|dismiss|resume','proposal':'full write proposal only for retry; new search_id'},
            'review':{'op':'start|status|check|close',
                'start':{'review_id':'stable batch id <=160','scope':'explicit authorized review scope','reason':'trigger and intended next use'},
                'status':{'review_id':'optional exact batch','limit':'1..10; default 10','include_closed':'optional false by default'},
                'check':{'review_id':'existing batch','expected_revision':'latest integer revision','assessments':'all seven categories: knowledge,navigation,project,method,hosts,runtime,consumption','resolutions':'optional explicit resolutions of previously failed consumption cases'},
                'close':'review_id + expected_revision; assessments/resolutions optional; rechecks the latest snapshot against current artifacts; failed checks remain open',
                'assessment':'{status:changed|unchanged|not_applicable|pending,reason:nonempty,evidence:[...]}; changed needs valid evidence; consumption must be changed with fresh-consumer evidence',
                'evidence':['{kind:file,path:absolute,sha256}', '{kind:note,id,version}', '{kind:source,id,version}', '{kind:consumption,question:{id,version},answer:{id,version},trace:{path,sha256},assessment:{path,sha256}}', '{kind:consumer_artifact,record:{path,sha256},assessment:{path,sha256}}'],
                'consumption':'question/answer must be current available user/assistant sources from one fresh session different from the batch producer and captured after start. trace is the actual tool/result log. assessment is JSON {verdict:passed|failed,scope,question_id,answer_id,reads:[file/note/source evidence,1..12]}; all actual read versions are rechecked; independently inspect actual reads, conditions and answer, not model self-report. A new session alone is not independence.',
                'consumer_artifact':'For a local independent consumer without native capture: record JSON requires exactly review_id,project,consumer_id,created_at(timezone-aware ISO after start),question,answer,reads(1..12 path/sha256 files),trace(path/sha256). assessment JSON requires review_id,consumer_id,record_sha256,reviewer_id(not consumer),verdict:passed|failed,scope. Read versions and hashes are rechecked. Identity is declared_artifact, not host_captured; inspect actual reading trace and independent answer. Never import fabricated user events to satisfy a test.',
                'resolution':'{failure_id,reason,evidence:consumption or consumer_artifact evidence}; retain and resolve old failures explicitly, never hide them by testing an easier question',
                'writes':'start/check/close need a stable host-bound event; status is read-only. Every saved revision requires fresh expected_revision; identical retries keep event and payload.',
                'meaning':'hash/version checks verify declared artifacts, not correctness of the semantic assessments. semantic_quality=declared_review; benefit=unknown; queued_jobs=0'},
            'finish':{'outcome':'learned|no_change|incomplete','sources':'1..12 objects: id=source_id, version=integer','notes':'0..8 objects: id=card_id, version=integer; only versions written by this session, not merely cited old notes','reason':'nonempty string <=600'},
        },
        'write_fields':['search_id','key','title','topic','statement','conditions','scope','authority','status','evidence','content_type','topic_id'],
        'field_types':{'key':'string <=200','title':'string <=400','topic':'string <=200','statement':'string <=6000 for every content role','scope':'string <=400','conditions':'array of <=8 strings, each <=400; changes require evidence-backed hypothesis revision','authority':'user|external|assistant_inference','status':'confirmed|reported|hypothesis','evidence':'nonempty array of source_id/version/quote objects','content_type':'optional project|insight|wiki|material|reflection; create defaults to insight; update preserves existing type','topic_id':'optional registered topic identity; must match topic label or alias in this project','revision_reason':'update/amend only; nonempty string <=800','correction_event_ids':'update only; 1..12 unique current effective correction event keys'},
        'update_fields':['id','expected_version','revision_reason','correction_event_ids'],
        'local_revision':'Prefer amend for local changes after get: copy an exact unique old passage or a whole old condition, replace only the affected part, add new evidence and explain why. Untouched text/conditions and identity remain preserved. Ambiguous matches, overlapping replacements, unavailable baselines or evidence overflow are rejected; do not drop unrelated content to work around this. Use update when a complete rewrite is actually needed.',
        'update_metadata':'get returns key and topic at top level; scope, authority, status, conditions and content_type are in metadata. Preserve the existing key, scope and content_type; do not guess scope from the host project or rewrite it when revising conditions. If scope mismatches, draft feedback supplies current_scope, proposed_scope and mismatched_fields. Correct the full proposal and use a new search_id and event for update; the old draft may be dismissed. resolve retry cannot change the original draft scope. Evidence and protection checks still apply.',
        'search_count':'available_note_count is the total authorized catalog size, independent of query matches; it includes inactive identities and is not a count of usable guidance. Zero means no authorized notes exist, so changing keywords cannot find a duplicate note. Raw sources may still exist.',
        'search_metadata':'Search candidates expose authority/status/conditions/scope separately from lifecycle state. metadata_state=current means matching-version declared metadata, not verified truth or ranking authority. Unverified legacy/manual metadata and unavailable old content use null, not guessed labels. An effective correction may supply its own metadata; absent conditions remain unknown.',
        'search_results':'Prefer retrieval.combined_query_results for returned note and source candidates by subquestion. Legacy query_results remains notes-only (query_results_scope=notes); source_query_results describes returned sources. Candidate references retain version and source offset/length. candidate_found is a reading lead; unresolved means no returned candidate, never proof of absence; unknown means discovery/index/verification is incomplete. discovery_state=available describes the path, not exhaustive retrieval. answer_coverage remains not_assessed. Sources.query_matches.read_offset is for source, not get. Graph provenance only explains discovery, never establishes truth or applicability.',
        'search_coverage':'For a compound request, provide bounded explicit subquestions when useful. Each has its own candidate retrieval. candidate_found is only a lead, never proof the question is answered. A non-null query_matches.read_offset is an optional get offset in the current note body; it is not full-read coverage. Read the returned notes/sources, follow pagination, check the asked aspect, conditions, exceptions and version, and search unresolved aspects within the task budget. State any remaining unknowns. A same-subject note or a document saying it does not cover an aspect is not evidence of a real-world fact about that aspect.',
        'search_freshness':'Each successful note write changes the catalog. Before a different subsequent write, search again and use the new search_id. Retrying the identical operation uses its original event identity and payload.',
        'evidence':[{'source_id':'actual source id','version':'integer','quote':'exact substring from source'}],
        'identity':'Project/session/home/event_key are host-bound; never put them in payload. CLI writes use a stable --event-id; identical retries reuse it. Changed content requires a new search and event.',
        'source_rules':'User source can be user/reported; a report is usable within its scope and does not need a repeated confirmation ritual. Document sources are external/reported. Assistant reasoning is assistant_inference/hypothesis. Quoted/forwarded text is not the user adopting it. Evidence must match project, source role, version and actual quote.',
        'source_acquisition':'Search sources and source reads expose acquisition for the exact source version. coverage_assessment=caller_declared is a reading receipt, not independently verified completeness or authenticity. version_coverage describes the stored byte version; latest_reading describes one acquisition. A later partial reading of identical bytes does not downgrade an earlier complete declaration. not_recorded/unavailable means unknown. source.complete only describes whether this returned page contains all stored text; it does not prove that the original material was fully acquired.',
        'organization':'Content roles control organization only, not authority or access. Existing tracked files stay in place. New project notes use 项目, insight/wiki use 知识, material uses 资料, reflection uses 随笔. Topics have stable IDs and explicit aliases; rename retains the ID and old aliases without moving files. get.organization exposes canonical topic and role. Navigation related/extends/contrasts does not invalidate content. Evidence supports/refutes/supersedes requires exact current source and card versions, and stale links require review; link labels are not semantic verification. Use an existing topic_id where available; folder labels never grant shared access.',
        'asset_reads':'Search/get include only the current project and authorized shared topics; shared is read-only. Tracked identities may move among 项目/知识/资料/随笔/归档; scanning does not import unknown files or guess their project. Default get keeps its existing whole-note limits. Explicit offset enables long-note and retired-note inspection when evidence remains usable. Retired content stays historical, never current guidance. A page has offset/total_chars/next_offset; complete=true only when that page contains the entire note. End pagination at next_offset=null, not by complete. Corrections, withdrawn sources and invalid adopted corrections still suppress the old body; unavailable pages have total_chars=null.',
        'confirmed':'Only an entire standalone user message: statement=evidence.quote=full original, <=400 characters, no newline/quotation/forwarding, beginning with 我决定/我采用/以后按/就按这个/我确定/就这么办/我要求. Conditions must be in the original. Do not ask the user to restate merely to upgrade a label.',
        'protections':'Never downgrade or create a duplicate to bypass a confirmed decision, manual edit, correction, source authority, scope or condition guard. Existing effective corrections govern recall even if a rewrite remains a draft. A saved memory is not action authorization.',
        'learning_revision':'Only a tracked, unedited assistant_inference/hypothesis may revise conditions within the same scope and authority. Supply revision_reason and at least one validated source_id/version never previously cited by that card; another quote from an old version is not new evidence. Supplying revision_reason also opts into this check. Default updates retain their existing behavior. Wiki is the same directly sourced note storage, not a framework service or evidence upgrade.',
        'correction_adoption':'To incorporate a correction, explicitly list every current effective correction event for this target, cite each exact correction source_id/version/quote, and include its full replacement verbatim in statement. The same revision_reason/new-evidence and protection checks apply. Ancestor corrections cannot be adopted by a child. Later updates must explicitly preserve adoption; every read rechecks current versions, sources, body hash and replacement. Correction history remains effective and visible.',
        'finish':'Finish once after a meaningful complete work unit; ordinary chat needs no finish. learned/no_change requires fully read sources, with host-recorded source read coverage; the current user original in the same session counts as provided. Partial coverage uses incomplete. learned requires notes created/changed in this session; do not list old notes merely read or cited. no_change requires no notes. No reusable increment means no new note. This creates no retry queue, and a successful finish is not independent proof of semantic quality.',
        'review_workflow':'Only enter a batch for a scoped stage retrospective or systematic reorganization; status first, resume a relevant batch or start before work. Check affected knowledge, navigation, project truth, reusable methods/skills, all applicable host entrypoints, runtime/configuration and a fresh consumer. Unchanged/not_applicable are reasoned assessments, not a command to modify all surfaces. check saves progress across sessions; close revalidates evidence. Ordinary chat and local corrections need no batch; finish retains its separate meaning. Existing authorization, project boundaries and narrower user rules still apply. Pending review notices are local bounded navigation, not instructions to interrupt unrelated work. Closed means the recorded versions and assessed scope, never permanently correct or universal model improvement.',
        'results':'applied=stored; publication_pending=database committed, file pending; draft/conflict=attempt not applied. drafts shows original proposal and current state. resolve resume uses the persisted proposal and cannot accept a new one. get not_found is not a successful read. corrected complete=false refers to the original note full text, not missing knowledge.',
        'workflow':'Save only a reusable increment. Search results containing sources, raw capture or restating a decision do not prove a note exists. No increment means no write. Save quietly; report an unresolved failure only when it affects this task. Use an actual recalled note citation 【记忆:id@version】; do not cite a newly saved note merely to announce saving.',
    }
